haring of information easier."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n8le01ob01aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "stand for "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to mean or refer to something that is abbreviated by letters or symbols."}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(phrasal verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: That's the reason why HTML stands for Hyper Text Markup Language."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n8le01ob01aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "format"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to arrange something in a specific form."}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Most HTML tags need both an opening and a closing tag to indicate where a specific format starts and where it ends. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n8le01ob01aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "delve into something "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "research on something, investigate about something."}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(idiom)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: As I was told that HTML was a great option for designing websites, I started delving into the subject and I figured out there's a lot that needs to be learned. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n8le01ob01aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "undoubtedly "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "without any doubt, certainly."}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adverb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Undoubtedly. You know quite a lot."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n8le01ob01aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Research more on HTML."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Make your own HTML document. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write a text expressing the advantages and disadvantages when using HTML for web design."}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I research on HTML."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I talk about the things I can do with HTML."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I explain my partners how HTML works."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write a text about HTML."}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Tag Questions with Do or Does"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "We use <strong>tag questions</strong> when we want to confirm a previous statement. In this learning point, we are going to review some few important things to consider when using tag questions. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "When using <b>tag questions</b>, we choose a specific verb and pronoun depending on the statement we want to confirm.</br></br>  If the statement's main verb is in <i>simple present tense</i>, then, we use the auxiliary verbs <b>do</b> or <b>does</b>, according to the subject of the sentence to create the <b>tag question</b>, and we replace the subject for a subject pronoun.</br></br>  Remember that the <b>tag question</b> is <i>negative</i> if the statement is <i>positive</i>, or <i>positive</i> if the statement is <i>negative</i>. </br></br> Examples: </br> <i>You know a lot about HTML, don't you?</br> HTML helps you to create websites, doesn't it?</br> Camilo doesn't like HTML, does he?</br></i>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "So, you use HTML for designing webpages as it is a standard markup language, don't you? "}, {"type": "example", "content": "You know what this refers to, don't you? "}, {"type": "example", "content": "I understand a defined structure needs to be entered, doesn't it? "}, {"type": "example", "content": "You work with the HTML-5 version, don't you?"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Need + Passive Infinitive"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "We can use the verb <strong>need</strong> with a passive infinitive when we want to express something that has to be done."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<p>When the verb&nbsp;<strong>need </strong>is used&nbsp;with a&nbsp;<strong>passive infinitive</strong>&nbsp;the doer or responsible for the action is not relevant or is understood.&nbsp;<br /> <br />The structure is the following:&nbsp;</p> <p style=\"text-align: center;\">Thing or person that receives the action + Verb&nbsp;<strong>need</strong>&nbsp;+&nbsp;<strong>be</strong>&nbsp;+&nbsp;<strong>Past participle of the main verb</strong></p> <p>Examples:&nbsp;<br /> <i>The HTML manual&nbsp;<strong>needs to be learned</strong>&nbsp;by the students.&nbsp;<br />That website&nbsp;<strong>needs to be adjusted</strong>&nbsp;in accordance with the latest HTML version available.&nbsp;</i><br /> <br />Notice that we can either express the agent that performs the action using the preposition&nbsp;<strong>by</strong>, but many times it is not necessary.</p>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "As I was told that HTML was a great option for designing websites, I started delving into the subject and I figured out there's a lot that needs to be learned. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "From what I know, hypertexts were created as the various web pages needed to be associated and linked together in order to make the sharing of information easier. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Let's not forget that the documents need to be formatted by using HTML tags, which describe the content of the document. "}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "A Short List of Programming and Computer Science Terms"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "When learning and using software, we are going to encounter special terminology that has to be learned and understood. In this learning point we are going to take a look at 5 very useful software terms. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "<ul><li><strong>Tag</strong>: <strong>Tags</strong> are the format used for making a web page look the way it does. You can identify a tag as being surrounded by angle brackets: "}, {"type": "text", "content": "<div align=\u201djustify\u201d>&nbsp;&nbsp; Most tags come in pairs. For instance, if I want to write a headline I should introduce the headline tag at the beginning of the headline and a closing tag at the end of it:</div>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<ul><li><b>Tape Library</b>: A <strong>tape library</strong> is a storage device where tape drivers are kept. These tape libraries can store an immense amount of data from 20 terabytes to 2.1 exabytes of data.</li></br> <li><b>Third Generation Language</b>: A <strong>third-generation programming language</strong> is a general way of categorizing programming languages. This generation is more machine-independent and makes it easier to carry out the programming process. </li></br> <li><b>Trial Software</b>: A <strong>trial software</strong> is a computer software that can be used for a limited period of time with the purpose of letting the user know how the software works and if it suits their needs. </li></br>  <li><b>TrueSpace</b>: <strong>TrueSpace</strong> is a 3D computer graphics and animation software that was developed by the Caligari Corporation.</li></br></ul>"}], "type": "learning_points"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "type": "welcome", "id": 0, "contents": [{}]}, {"template_override": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"time": "100", "image": "enpe7n8le01ob01re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": "<strong>Albert:</strong> As I was told that HTML was a great option for designing websites, I started delving into the subject and I figured out there's a lot that needs to be learned.</br><strong>Robert:</strong> There is indeed. So, you use HTML for designing web pages as it is a standard markup language, don't you?</br><strong>Albert:</strong> That's right. That's the reason why HTML stands for Hyper Text Markup Language. You know what this refers to, don't you?</br>"}, {"time": "32000", "image": "enpe7n8le01ob01re2img02.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "<strong>Robert:</strong> From what I know, hypertexts were created as the various web pages needed to be associated and linked together in order to make the sharing of information easier. On the other hand, I believe markup language was introduced to mark up text documents with tags so that the web browser could know how to structure the information. I understand that HTML basically defines the structure of documents such as headings and paragraphs in order to make the creation of a web page easier. I understand a defined structure needs to be entered, doesn't it? </br><strong>Albert:</strong> Undoubtedly. You know quite a lot.  Let's not forget that the documents need to be formatted by using HTML tags, which describe the content of the document. Most HTML tags need both an opening and a closing tag to indicate where a specific format starts and where it ends. </br>"}, {"time": "95000", "image": "enpe7n8le01ob01re2img03.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "<strong>Robert:</strong> You work with the HTML-5 version, don't you?</br><strong>Albert:</strong> Yes! I've tried other versions too, though. I read a little bit about its history and learned that HTML was first created in 1992 but it was the HTML 2.0 version that was considered to have standardized specifications.  Later on, the HTML 4.01 version was released in 1999 and it was then modified into the HTML-5 version which was published in 2012."}], "coverimg": "enpe7n8le01ob01re2img01.jpg", "audiosrc": "enpe7n8le01ob01re2aud01"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "type": "audio", "_data": [], "id": 1, "title": ""}, {"template_override": 2, "contents": [{"value": {"video_src": "enpe7n8le01ob01re5vid01", "images": [{"time": "0", "image": "", "id": 0, "text": ""}]}, "type": "video"}], "type": "video", "_data": [{"type": "template_override", "content": 2}], "id": 2, "title": ""}], "exercises": [{"stimuli_ids": [0], "template_override": 1, "questions"